# Hooks and utils placement

Hooks and utilities that are (or will be) used outside their defining module live in separate files under `hooks/` or `utils/`.

- If the hook/util is tied to one feature or component, colocate it next to that component:
  `ComponentName/hooks/useSomething.ts`, `ComponentName/utils/formatSomething.ts`.
- If it looks useful in multiple places, put it in a more general folder:
  `hooks/useSomething.ts`, `lib/utils/...` / top-level `utils/` as the project already uses.
- Do not export hooks or shared utils from the component file itself.
- Helpers used only inside one file stay in that file and are not exported.
- Hook files are named after the hook (`useTelegram.ts`). Util files use camelCase names matching the util.

```tsx
// BAD — hook exported from the component module
// TelegramProvider.tsx
export default TelegramProvider
export { useTelegram }

import { useTelegram } from "@/components/providers/TelegramProvider/TelegramProvider"

// GOOD — hook in a hooks folder next to the feature
// TelegramProvider/hooks/useTelegram.ts
export { useTelegram }

import { useTelegram } from "@/components/providers/TelegramProvider/hooks/useTelegram"
```
